{"task_id": "HumanEval/46", "solution": "```python\ndef fib4(n: int):\n    \"\"\"Computes the n-th element of the Fib4 number sequence using an iterative approach.\"\"\"\n    if n == 0 or n == 1:\n        return 0\n    elif n == 2:\n        return 2\n    elif n == 3:\n        return 0\n\n    # Initialize the last four Fib4 numbers: fib4(0), fib4(1), fib4(2), fib4(3)\n    f0, f1, f2, f3 = 0, 0, 2, 0\n\n    for i in range(4, n + 1):\n        # Calculate the next Fib4 number\n        current_fib4 = f3 + f2 + f1 + f0\n        # Shift values to prepare for the next iteration\n        f0 = f1\n        f1 = f2\n        f2 = f3\n        f3 = current_fib4\n\n    return f3\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/44", "solution": "```python\ndef change_base(x: int, base: int):\n    \"\"\"Change numerical base of input number x to base.\n    return string representation after the conversion.\n    base numbers are less than 10.\n    >>> change_base(8, 3)\n    '22'\n    >>> change_base(8, 2)\n    '1000'\n    >>> change_base(7, 2)\n    '111'\n    \"\"\"\n\n    class InvalidBaseError(ValueError):\n        \"\"\"Custom exception for invalid base values.\"\"\"\n        def __init__(self, message: str = \"Base must be less than 10\"):\n            super().__init__(message)\n\n    def _validate_base(base: int) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Validates that the target base is less than 10.\"\"\"\n        if base >= 10:\n            raise InvalidBaseError(\"Base must be less than 10\")\n\n    def _convert_to_base(number: int, base: int) -> str:\n        \"\"\"Performs the core numerical conversion of an integer to the specified base.\"\"\"\n        if number == 0:\n            return \"0\"\n\n        result_digits = []\n        while number > 0:\n            remainder = number % base\n            result_digits.append(str(remainder))\n            number //= base\n\n        return \"\".join(result_digits[::-1])\n\n    _validate_base(base)\n    return _convert_to_base(x, base)\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/47", "solution": "```python\ndef median(l: list):\n    \"\"\"Return median of elements in the list l.\"\"\"\n    sorted_l = sorted(l)\n    n = len(sorted_l)\n\n    if n % 2 == 1:\n        # For odd-sized lists, the median is the middle element.\n        return float(sorted_l[n // 2])\n    else:\n        # For even-sized lists, the median is the average of the two middle elements.\n        mid1 = sorted_l[n // 2 - 1]\n        mid2 = sorted_l[n // 2]\n        return (float(mid1) + float(mid2)) / 2.0\n```"}
