{"task_id": "HumanEval/50", "solution": "```python\ndef decode_shift(s: str):\n    \"\"\"\n    Decodes a string by shifting each lowercase alphabetic character back by 5 positions, with 'a' to 'z' wrapping.\n    Non-alphabetic characters remain unchanged.\n    \"\"\"\n    decoded_chars = []\n    for char in s:\n        if 'a' <= char <= 'z':\n            shifted_ord = ord(char) - 5\n            if shifted_ord < ord('a'):\n                shifted_ord += 26\n            decoded_chars.append(chr(shifted_ord))\n        else:\n            decoded_chars.append(char)\n    return \"\".join(decoded_chars)\n```"}
